   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Make KEYFRAME B with the existing aiofm_i2i_qwen_zimage\nworkflow (Qwen-Edit branch), feeding KEYFRAME A as input:\n\n  \"same woman, same room, same lighting, she now holds the\n  t-shirt in her hand, wearing black tank top, hair slightly\n  mussed\"\n\nWHY THIS WORKS\nAn end-state keyframe that already shows the CONSEQUENCE of\nthe action (garment in hand / on floor, mussed hair) forces\nthe video model to act out the physical change. If B is just\n'same pose, different outfit', the model takes the lazy path:\na crossfade/morph where clothes dissolve.\n\nKEYFRAME B CHECKLIST\n\u2022 identical room, framing and lighting as A\n\u2022 the removed garment VISIBLE (in hand or on floor)\n\u2022 small secondary evidence: mussed hair, shifted stance\n\u2022 same 9:16 crop \u2014 both keyframes get scaled to 480\u00d7832,\n  mismatched aspect ratios cause stretching"
   ],
   "title": "\u2462 KEYFRAME B RECIPE (Qwen-Edit)",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    0,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 23,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Describe the PHYSICAL ACTION explicitly, with both hands,\nstart \u2192 middle \u2192 end, then the end state. Template:\n\n  \"She grips the hem of her [garment] with both hands,\n  pulls it up and over her head in one continuous smooth\n  motion, her hair falls back onto her shoulders, she lowers\n  her arms and holds it loosely in her right hand at her\n  side, now wearing [end-state outfit], natural fluid body\n  movement, static camera, soft indoor lighting,\n  photorealistic, natural skin texture\"\n\nRULES\n\u2022 name BOTH hands and the grip point (hem, waistband, strap)\n\u2022 one continuous verb chain: grips \u2192 pulls \u2192 lowers \u2192 holds\n\u2022 end the prompt on the END STATE outfit, never on the\n  removed garment (see note \u2464)\n\u2022 keep the camera static \u2014 camera moves + wardrobe change\n  in one clip doubles the failure rate"
   ],
   "title": "\u2463 MOTION PROMPT TEMPLATE",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    520,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 24,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "1) CROSSFADE / MORPH \u2014 clothes dissolve instead of being\n   pulled off. THE most common failure.\n   FIX: make KEYFRAME B more explicit about the end state\n   (garment clearly in hand/on floor, hair mussed) and\n   RESEED (change noise_seed on SAMPLER 1/2). This shot\n   type lands in 2\u20135 attempts \u2014 that is normal, budget\n   for it. Iterate at 480\u00d7832 (note \u2460).\n\n2) ANATOMY CHAOS MID-PULL \u2014 extra arms / melted torso while\n   the garment is over the face.\n   FIX: ONE garment per 81-frame clip, never two. Loose\n   garments (oversized tee, open shirt, robe) are much\n   easier than tight ones. Tight jeans/bodysuits: don't.\n\n3) REMOVED GARMENT RE-APPEARS at the end of the clip.\n   FIX: never mention the removed garment LATE in the\n   prompt \u2014 the tail of the prompt dominates the tail of\n   the clip. Name it once early (the grip), then only\n   describe the end-state outfit."
   ],
   "title": "\u2464 FAILURE MODES + FIXES",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    1040,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 25,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "PRESET A \u2014 MAX QUALITY (current defaults; finals)\n  \u26a1 Lightning LoRAs: BYPASSED (purple)\n  HIGH sampler: steps 20 \u00b7 cfg 3.5 \u00b7 start 0 \u00b7 end 10\n  LOW  sampler: steps 20 \u00b7 cfg 3.5 \u00b7 start 10 \u00b7 end 10000\n  Shift (both): 8.0\n\nPRESET B \u2014 LIGHTNING (drafts, \u224810\u00d7 faster)\n  Select both \u26a1 LoRA nodes \u2192 Ctrl+B to activate\n  HIGH sampler: steps 4 \u00b7 cfg 1.0 \u00b7 start 0 \u00b7 end 2\n  LOW  sampler: steps 4 \u00b7 cfg 1.0 \u00b7 start 2 \u00b7 end 10000\n  Shift (both): 5.0\n\n\u26a0 MOTION SUPPRESSION WARNING\nLightning LoRAs damp large motions \u2014 and a wardrobe change\nIS a large motion. Lightning drafts crossfade far more often\nand tell you little about whether a seed will act the pull\nproperly. Use Lightning only to sanity-check framing and\nkeyframe match; judge motion and pick seeds on PRESET A."
   ],
   "title": "\u2465 QUALITY VS SPEED",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    1560,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 26,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "One 81-frame clip = ONE garment (note \u2464). For a sequence\n(tee off \u2192 pants off \u2192 ...), chain segments:\n\n  seg 1: A = dressed still,  B = tee-in-hand still\n  seg 2: A = tee-in-hand still, B = pants-on-floor still\n  concat with ffmpeg afterwards.\n\nTHE RULE: every segment's keyframes must be CLEAN QWEN-EDIT\nSTILLS (note \u2462), NEVER decoded video frames. A decoded last\nframe carries VAE color drift + motion blur; feed it back in\nand each segment gets progressively more washed out and soft.\nInstead: Qwen-Edit the ORIGINAL still into each intermediate\nstate, so every segment starts from a first-generation image.\nKeep seed fixed per segment once it works; expect to reseed\neach segment independently (2\u20135 attempts each).\n\nIdentity: re-anchor every segment from the same original\nstill \u2014 this also prevents identity drift across the chain."
   ],
   "title": "\u2466 CHAINING \u2014 MULTI-GARMENT",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
 ],
